{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(4,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-36333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(4,-1,3):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})k \\\\  & =x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j-2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(4,-1,3) & =(4)\\text{ }i+2(-1)\\text{ }j-2(3)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-2,\\,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,-1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-(-1),\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-2,\\,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)-2(y+1)-6(z-3) & =0 \\\\ 4x-2y-6z & =0 \\\\ 2x-y-3z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-36333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5129adf3751dcc5fc70f5b0705243122ff442eabcb934251a274e2e55c971553"} {"question" "q-36333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-36333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-y-3z=0"] ["math" "x+2y-6z+14=0"] ["math" "x+2y-6z=0"] ["math" "x-2y+3z-15=0"] ["math" "x-y-3z+5=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-36333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x-y-3z=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+8y\\text{ }j+4z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+8(1)j+4(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+8\\,j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,8,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)+8(y-1)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x+8y+4z-20 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5129adf3751dcc5fc70f5b0705243122ff442eabcb934251a274e2e55c971553"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+8y+z-13=0"] ["math" "2x+y+z-6=0"] ["math" "x+2y+z-5=0"] ["math" "x+4y+4z-10=0"] ["math" "x+8y+4z-14=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+2y+z-5=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }i+(2y{x}^{3}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+2yzk \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-1,1) & =3(1)^{2}(-1)^{2}\\text{ }i+(\\,2(-1)(1)^{3}+(1)^{2}\\,)\\text{ }j+2(-1)(1)k \\\\  & =3\\,i-1\\,j-2k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5129adf3751dcc5fc70f5b0705243122ff442eabcb934251a274e2e55c971553"} {"question" "q-80764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3ed600fb83ad95d81e64a0081f2a44fcdbffef"} {"question" "q-80764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y+1,\\,z+2⟩=0"] ["math" "⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩=0"] ["math" "⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070916/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7acd2f87bb66e2eada5b47d7f3